{%- liquid
  # The subheading is authored as one short sentence per step — "Choose the
  # club. Film the view. Work one measured plan." As a paragraph that protocol
  # read as filler under the headline; split on the sentence break it becomes
  # the hairline rail below, out of the SAME authored setting. No second
  # setting to keep in sync, and nothing duplicated from the bands above.
  # Copy authored as one long sentence renders as one cell, which is still
  # correct — the split degrades into the paragraph it started as.
  # '||' is the join delimiter because prose never contains it; a single
  # character would eventually collide with real copy.
  assign sequence_parts = section.settings.sub | strip | split: '.'
  assign sequence = ''
  for part in sequence_parts
    assign step = part | strip
    if step != blank
      assign sequence = sequence | append: step | append: '||'
    endif
  endfor
  assign sequence = sequence | split: '||'

  # The old markup pointed a dead `#` at the primary action whenever the link
  # setting was empty — which is exactly what /pages/about ships, since
  # templates/page.about.json renders this section with no settings at all.
  # A button that goes nowhere is worse than no button, so each action now
  # renders only once it has somewhere to go.
  assign primary_url = section.settings.primary_url

  # Same fix on the secondary, but it has a real fallback: the Pro product.
  # Resolving through the product object rather than hardcoding
  # '/products/swinglab-pro' keeps the localised route and yields blank —
  # not a 404 — if the product is ever unpublished or renamed.
  assign secondary_url = section.settings.secondary_url
  if secondary_url == blank
    assign pro_product = all_products['swinglab-pro']
    if pro_product.handle != blank
      assign secondary_url = pro_product.url
    endif
  endif

  assign show_primary = false
  if section.settings.primary_label != blank and primary_url != blank
    assign show_primary = true
  endif
  assign show_secondary = false
  if section.settings.secondary_label != blank and secondary_url != blank
    assign show_secondary = true
  endif

  assign cta_title_id = 'CtaTitle-' | append: section.id
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  THE TERMINAL BAND. Every section above this one presents a reading; this is
  where the tape ends and the instrument hands back. So it is the quietest
  surface on the page rather than the loudest: it sits in the sunk well, it
  carries no amber and no cyan, and its only ornament is a ruled edge.

  That absence is deliberate, not an oversight. Amber marks a value the engine
  measured and cyan marks the live readout — a closing call to action is
  neither, so a signal colour here would be decoration, and decoration is the
  one thing those two colours are never allowed to be.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="sl-cta" aria-labelledby="{{ cta_title_id }}">
  <div class="sl-wrap">
    <div class="sl-cta__inner">
      {%- comment -%}
        Marginalia, set in the gutter like the notations down the edge of a
        spec sheet. It is a printed label rather than a heading, so it never
        enters the heading outline.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sl-cta__margin">
        {%- if section.settings.stamp != blank -%}
          <p class="sl-cta__stamp">{{ section.settings.stamp }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <span class="sl-cta__ticks" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="sl-cta__body sl-reveal">
        <h2 id="{{ cta_title_id }}" class="sl-cta__title">{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Your next range session should count.' }}</h2>

        {%- if sequence.size > 0 -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            role="list" is not redundant here: Safari drops list semantics from
            any list styled with list-style: none, and this one is. The printed
            ordinals only restate the list order for sighted readers, so they
            stay aria-hidden rather than being announced twice.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <ol class="sl-cta__sequence" role="list">
            {%- for step in sequence -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign ordinal = forloop.index
                if ordinal < 10
                  assign ordinal = ordinal | prepend: '0'
                endif
              -%}
              <li class="sl-cta__step">
                <span class="sl-cta__step-num" aria-hidden="true">{{ ordinal }}</span>
                <span class="sl-cta__step-text">{{ step }}</span>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ol>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The row itself is conditional, not just its children: an empty
          .sl-cta__actions still carries its top margin, which would leave an
          unexplained gap between the rail and the fine print.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if show_primary or show_secondary -%}
          <div class="sl-cta__actions">
            {%- if show_primary -%}
              <a href="{{ primary_url }}"
                 class="sl-btn sl-cta__primary"
                 data-app-primary-cta
                 data-app-signed-out-label="{{ section.settings.primary_label | escape }}"
                 data-app-signed-out-url="{{ primary_url }}">
                {%- comment -%}
                  header.liquid rewrites [data-app-cta-label] when it has one and
                  falls back to overwriting the whole node's textContent when it
                  does not — so the arrow only survives because the label has its
                  own span. Do not flatten these two.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <span data-app-cta-label>{{ section.settings.primary_label }}</span>
                <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if show_secondary -%}
              <a href="{{ secondary_url }}"
                 class="sl-btn sl-cta__secondary"
                 data-app-pro-sales-link>{{ section.settings.secondary_label }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.fine_print != blank -%}
          <p class="sl-cta__fine">{{ section.settings.fine_print }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* The well, not the field. The page darkens by one step at the end, which is
   what separates this band from its neighbours without adding a single
   decorative colour. The 8px instrument grid is repainted locally because the
   well's own background would otherwise cover the one on <body>. */
.sl-cta {
  position: relative;
  isolation: isolate;
  background:
    linear-gradient(rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.022) 1px, transparent 1px),
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.022) 1px, transparent 1px),
    var(--sl-night);
  background-size: 8px 8px, 8px 8px, auto;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
  padding: var(--sl-section-space) 0 var(--sl-section-space-compact);
}
/* The ruled edge — the graduated lip of a measuring face. Two repeating
   gradients so the scale has major and minor ticks; one gradient can only
   draw ticks of a single height. */
.sl-cta::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  height: 12px;
  pointer-events: none;
  background-image:
    repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.2) 0 1px, transparent 1px 48px),
    repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.09) 0 1px, transparent 1px 8px);
  background-size: 100% 12px, 100% 6px;
  background-position: bottom left, bottom left;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
}

.sl-cta__inner {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--sl-space-5);
}
/* Asymmetric, and the gutter is a real rule rather than a gap: the margin
   column gets the border and the grid gap goes to zero, so the hairline runs
   the full height of the band the way a ruled column does on paper. */
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-cta__inner {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 176px) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
  }
}

.sl-cta__margin {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--sl-space-4);
}
.sl-cta__stamp {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-eyebrow-size);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: var(--sl-eyebrow-track);
  line-height: 1;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
/* The stamp's scale bar. On phones it runs across to the edge of the wrap; in
   the desktop gutter it stands up and runs down the column. */
.sl-cta__ticks {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  height: 6px;
  background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.16) 0 1px, transparent 1px 8px);
}
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-cta__margin {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding-right: var(--sl-space-5);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  }
  .sl-cta__ticks {
    width: 6px;
    height: auto;
    min-height: var(--sl-space-9);
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.16) 0 1px, transparent 1px 8px);
  }
}

.sl-cta__body { min-width: 0; }
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-cta__body { padding-left: clamp(28px, 3vw, 56px); }
}
.sl-cta__title {
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 20ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-heading-display);
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  line-height: 1.02;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-wrap: balance;
}

/* The protocol as a spec strip: 1px gaps over the hairline colour, cells in
   the raised panel. Shadows are invisible on a near-black field, so the
   separation has to come from the border showing through the gaps. */
.sl-cta__sequence {
  margin: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px) 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
@media (min-width: 560px) {
  .sl-cta__sequence { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-cta__sequence { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
}
.sl-cta__step {
  display: grid;
  align-content: start;
  gap: var(--sl-space-2);
  padding: var(--sl-dense-inset);
  background: var(--sl-bg-card);
}
.sl-cta__step-num {
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  line-height: 1;
}
.sl-cta__step-text {
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  line-height: 1.45;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

.sl-cta__actions {
  margin: clamp(26px, 3vw, 36px) 0 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: var(--sl-space-3);
}
/* header.liquid hides the Pro sales link for members by setting the hidden
   attribute. .sl-btn's display: inline-flex outranks the UA's [hidden] rule,
   so without this the link stayed visible to the members it is meant to skip
   — the same latent bug main-product.liquid already fixed for its price. */
.sl-cta__actions [hidden] { display: none; }
.sl-cta__primary,
.sl-cta__secondary {
  min-height: 52px;
  padding: 14px 24px;
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-control);
  font-weight: 600;
}
/* Bone, matching the hero's primary exactly — the page's two main actions are
   the same control and must not drift apart. Amber marks a measured value; a
   button is not one. */
.sl-cta__primary {
  border-color: var(--sl-ink);
  background: var(--sl-ink);
  color: var(--sl-bg);
}
.sl-cta__primary:hover {
  border-color: var(--sl-trace);
  background: var(--sl-trace);
  color: var(--sl-bg);
}
/* --sl-control-border, never --sl-border: this is the sole edge of an
   interactive control and the decorative hairline is 1.33:1. */
.sl-cta__secondary {
  border-color: var(--sl-control-border);
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
}
.sl-cta__secondary:hover {
  border-color: var(--sl-ink);
  background: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.06);
  color: var(--sl-ink);
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .sl-cta__primary span:last-child { transition: transform .2s ease; }
  .sl-cta__primary:hover span:last-child { transform: translateX(4px); }
}

/* The status line at the foot of a printout: mono, uppercase, held short so
   it wraps into a stamp rather than running on as a paragraph. */
.sl-cta__fine {
  margin: var(--sl-space-5) 0 0;
  max-width: 54ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 400;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  line-height: 1.6;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

@media (max-width: 749px) {
  .sl-cta__title { max-width: 100%; }
  /* Full-bleed stacked actions: side-by-side buttons on a phone put both
     targets under the same thumb. */
  .sl-cta__actions { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "CTA banner",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "stamp",
      "label": "Margin stamp",
      "info": "Mono label set in the gutter, like the notation on a spec sheet.",
      "default": "End of readout"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Your next range session should count." },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "sub",
      "label": "Protocol",
      "info": "One short sentence per step. Each sentence renders as its own cell in the numbered rail.",
      "default": "Choose the club. Film the view. Work one measured plan. Re‑film by repeating the setup."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "primary_label", "label": "Primary button label", "default": "Analyze a swing free" },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "primary_url",
      "label": "Primary button link",
      "info": "Required — the button is hidden rather than pointed at a dead link."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "secondary_label", "label": "Secondary button label", "default": "Get Pro" },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "secondary_url",
      "label": "Secondary button link",
      "info": "Defaults to the CaddieInsight Pro product page."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "fine_print",
      "label": "Fine print",
      "default": "No card required · One analysis and one matched re-film each month"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "CTA banner" }]
}
{% endschema %}
